WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.178 --> 00:00:12.080
Latria. Once an ivory tower, now, the city has&nbsp;
become the stuff of nightmares. New prisoners are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:18.320
locked up and tortured in the Prison of Hope, then&nbsp;
told to seek redemption up above. There is none.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:23.920
Instead, gargoyles take them to the upper city,&nbsp;
where they will inevitably join the rest of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:29.840
bodies dumped into a sea of flesh and blood.&nbsp;
Tentacles absorb the repulsive mix of remains,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:37.200
feeding a gargantuan ball of flesh. This heart&nbsp;
of Latria spits out chimeric abominations,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:40.800
each with the face of a former&nbsp;
prisoner, contorted in agony.
&nbsp;

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:46.000
Behind it all is the Golden Elder, a&nbsp;
former noble. Consequences be damned,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:47.969
he will have his revenge.
Rydell screams, echoes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.969 --> 00:00:50.960
as the video begins. 
In Demon's Souls, magic benefits from one's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:56.400
intelligence. The more clearly you are able to&nbsp;
comprehend something, the more powerful your magic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:02.400
becomes. Latria clearly had a focus on science&nbsp;
and experimentation - look to the equipment in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:07.760
their towers, and even on their archstone..for&nbsp;
proof of that. It set them apart from others&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:13.440
known to have practiced the Soul Arts - like&nbsp;
the Monumentals, who practiced through faith 
&nbsp;

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:18.160
That's not to say that Latria didn't have a&nbsp;
culture of worship as well. They absolutely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:23.840
did. Look at what's depicted on the queen's&nbsp;
throne - a woman representing royal authority,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:29.760
her body emanating light while a Pegasus glides&nbsp;
through the heavens; all symbols of divinity and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:36.560
spiritual freedom. The Queen was the holiest of&nbsp;
holies, a being of supreme magical and therefore:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:43.520
divine power. The bridge between man, and god.&nbsp;
Perhaps they were looking to cross that bridge.
&nbsp;

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:48.880
The researchers and sages of the Ivory&nbsp;
Tower elevated themselves to aristocrat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:52.329
believing they deserved to enjoy the finer things&nbsp;
as well [[Silverwork Bracelets, Aged Spice,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.329 --> 00:01:56.640
Fresh Spice]]. For who better to stand beside&nbsp;
the Queen, than men of similar knowledge?
&nbsp;

00:01:56.640 --> 00:02:00.240
I was once the wife of nobility, and I&nbsp;
have some nice things to show for it.
&nbsp;

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:07.840
To be clear - these were not royals, they were&nbsp;
nobles. Not family, but clan. Thus, since they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:14.000
weren't born into power, it was possible to obtain&nbsp;
it. One way was to strive to be intelligent,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:18.480
like the queen [[monumental dialogue]], but&nbsp;
another was to simply become wealthier. Though..&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:23.440
when your currency is souls, that can&nbsp;
quickly become a dark desire indeed. 
&nbsp;

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:29.120
The Silver Bracelets we find in Latria boost&nbsp;
the amount of souls you receive, and they're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:31.904
an example of how the rich get richer. Mankind is&nbsp;
greedy, always lusting for more, and some, like a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.904 --> 00:02:34.480
certain old man, would do anything to ascend.
It was this exact same lust for power,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:40.480
that triggered the First Scourge. But it&nbsp;
wasn't Latria that triggered that. Instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:44.000
it was the Monumentals. 
Luckily, the Old One was sealed away&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:50.240
by the same monumentals - and the world learned&nbsp;
to fear the power they had toyed with. And even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:56.400
though it was the bedrock of their society,&nbsp;
Latria joined them in forbidding such knowledge.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:02.720
The Ivory Tower's magical studies were over.&nbsp;
Without something to strive for, they were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:09.840
bereft of direction. All they had now, was&nbsp;
their queen, and a backstabbing aristocracy. 
&nbsp;

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:16.880
During this age, Latria became a dangerous&nbsp;
place indeed. Assassination became a part of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:21.040
their political culture, and the weapons&nbsp;
that facilitate these dark deeds can be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:23.760
found all throughout the city [[Mercury Rapier,&nbsp;
Baby's Nail, Needle of Eternal Agony]]. Nobles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:30.000
famously took to wearing the red lotus; partly&nbsp;
for its beauty, but mostly because it's a quick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:34.560
cure for poison [[Noble's Lotus]]. Even&nbsp;
absent magic, man's malice remained.
&nbsp;

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:41.680
Far better suited to this post-magic world&nbsp;
was Boletaria, whose raw military strength&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:47.600
allowed them to expand their borders. Evidence&nbsp;
of their spies can even be found within Latria,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:51.840
suggesting the Ivory Tower might&nbsp;
have been next on their list. 
&nbsp;

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:58.080
Luckily for Latria, the Soul was rediscovered&nbsp;
by Boletaria, who flourished thanks to its arts.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:03.360
In order to tip the scales back in their favour,&nbsp;
the Queen made the decision to restore the Ivory&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:09.920
Tower - restart research which had for so long&nbsp;
collected dust. Latria would once again become&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:15.840
a beacon of academia, and this time, it was&nbsp;
a wise man named Freke who led the way. 
&nbsp;

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:21.120
A former priest, Freke systemised the Soul&nbsp;
Arts into an academic framework for anyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:27.920
to learn He is known as the "Sage of Yormedaar",&nbsp;
a distinguished school in Latria where the rich&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.920 --> 00:04:33.360
and privileged from all over came to learn the&nbsp;
soul arts - including you, if you chose a noble&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:38.960
background. Freke would go on to travel, spreading&nbsp;
his methods and the fame of the Yormedaar school&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:44.800
far and wide. Now, in this new world where&nbsp;
magic was allowed, Latria had power and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:53.120
influence - even gifting ornate armaments to a&nbsp;
certain prince of Boletaria when he came touring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:57.520
in its borders. They were finally safe&nbsp;
from external forces like Boletaria..but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.320 --> 00:05:02.240
turns out, it was those at home that they&nbsp;
should have been more concerned about.
&nbsp;

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:08.160
Among the noble researchers, there&nbsp;
was an elderly man who went too far.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:12.480
His obsession with souls crossed the&nbsp;
line, and he likely even dabbled in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.480 --> 00:05:16.080
human experimentation [[Source: his later&nbsp;
exploits]], extracting vast amount of souls from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:22.320
others . You'll recall - it was this exact same&nbsp;
thirst for power that awoke the Old One eons ago.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:32.320
So, the Queen banished this high-ranking member&nbsp;
of the Ivory Tower. It was the right thing to do,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.320 --> 00:05:42.000
but it couldn't have backfired more horribly.
Around this time, during his exile, the Old One&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:43.680
was awoken by the exact same lust for power&nbsp;
in King Allant of Boletaria, which triggered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.680 --> 00:05:50.000
the second scourge. Demons returned to the&nbsp;
land, and as if like magic, a golden cloth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:59.120
emerged from the fog - a demon, with the power&nbsp;
to make the elderly man's dreams a reality. 
&nbsp;

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:02.640
The Queen banished her depraved&nbsp;
old man from the land.
&nbsp;

00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:08.480
He returned in strange golden&nbsp;
garb with foul Demons in tow.
&nbsp;

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:15.760
They pillaged great Latria, land of the&nbsp;
learned, and shut us away in this prision.
&nbsp;

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:21.120
Garbed in that regal colour, the old&nbsp;
man ravaged Latria, killed its Queen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:26.480
and and imprisoned all who were a part of her&nbsp;
ruling clan. To help enforce his new rule, broken&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.480 --> 00:06:32.080
servants channel rudimentary spells throughout the&nbsp;
city, sustaining a horrific system of sacrifice.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:38.160
They are protected by former noblemen who&nbsp;
forsook their pride and patriotism to join&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:43.600
the winning side - Magicians, who transformed&nbsp;
into the octopus-headed Jailers, still carrying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.600 --> 00:06:49.840
expensive spices, and wearing their old robes.
Since then, they've been feeding off our souls…
&nbsp;

00:06:50.960 --> 00:06:56.480
Telling us over and over that if we go&nbsp;
above, we will be granted redemption.
&nbsp;

00:06:57.360 --> 00:07:02.720
The Queen is alive, they say. Right there in&nbsp;
the church up above. Go up and see for yourself.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:08.320
She is immortal, rising over and over again.&nbsp;
Those who survive the cruel torture and traps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:13.440
arrive to praise their undying goddess, never&nbsp;
noticing the servant pulling the strings.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:20.240
To a hopeless, soul-siphoned Latrian,&nbsp;
it must sound all too tempting. 
&nbsp;

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:28.080
Then come the gargoyles, the souls of Latrian&nbsp;
soldiers and knights inserted in the local&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:34.400
statues, to drag worshippers of this Fool’s&nbsp;
Idol up to the horror behind the holy veneer.
&nbsp;

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:40.160
The old man is making the prisoners take part&nbsp;
in his perverse experiments - creating demons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:45.360
and fulfilling his role as an archdemon of the&nbsp;
Old One. No one can stop his revenge. Not even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:50.800
Freke himself, who returns to Latria only&nbsp;
to be locked up in a cell like the rest.
&nbsp;

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:54.640
I was defeated and captured by the&nbsp;
golden elder beyond that dungeon.
&nbsp;

00:07:55.520 --> 00:08:04.480
Beware of him, for he manipulates souls.
He has power over dark souls,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.120 --> 00:08:11.840
those susceptible to madness and paranoia.
The Elder may be powerful, yet the golden cloth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:18.080
he wears is still a demon. Its power is not his&nbsp;
own, and his soul hardly matches its appetite. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:22.960
cloth seeks a new vessel to control with paranoia&nbsp;
and mania, and will abandon the old man to die&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:29.520
once it has found that more worthy body.
For..the goal of Demonkind is not to elevate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:34.640
humanity to their status. It's to wipe&nbsp;
them out and obscure everything in fog.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.640 --> 00:08:39.840
That's the cost of power here, and for&nbsp;
some, it's a worthy price to pay. 
&nbsp;

00:08:40.560 --> 00:08:43.520
Why, you have defeated all&nbsp;
the demons, have you not?
&nbsp;

00:08:44.240 --> 00:08:49.440
This ghastly howl. The Monumental&nbsp;
has spoken of it before…
&nbsp;

00:08:50.560 --> 00:08:57.840
There is a question I have long had in my mind
It is whether we are right to banish the Old One
&nbsp;

00:08:59.520 --> 00:09:04.640
And I now have the answer,&nbsp;
and it is a resounding no.
&nbsp;

00:09:06.240 --> 00:09:10.880
Listen closely. The Old One&nbsp;
must not be cut off from us.
&nbsp;

00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:15.600
If the candle maiden tries&nbsp;
to entrap it, kill her.
&nbsp;

00:09:16.640 --> 00:09:21.000
Then Absorb the souls of&nbsp;
the Old One for yourself.
&nbsp;

00:09:21.840 --> 00:09:29.200
The Old one is an unfathomable deposit of energy,&nbsp;
it contains all the souls collected by the Demons
&nbsp;

00:09:30.400 --> 00:09:35.840
You will gain the power of a King, and&nbsp;
I will gain knowledge from beyond.
&nbsp;

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:40.720
And that, my dear friend, is the righteous path.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.840 --> 00:09:44.640
You must not allow trifling&nbsp;
matters to dissuade you.
&nbsp;

00:09:45.440 --> 00:10:01.840
The Demon souls shall be ours!
